#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718822 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fda3e26-e4c6-5c00-9e46-5c81c4f7242a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 t + 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718812} {:answer/id #uuid "69408d0a-116c-5fa2-9b9e-da596e68771f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718815} {:answer/id #uuid "983e2684-5ddf-5ab8-899b-a139d2958aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718823} {:answer/id #uuid "d77921f1-e700-5f5e-9c0d-03a82421b451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 t + 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718832} {:answer/id #uuid "f8eec515-d108-5724-860f-b6cc1f07d9c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "983e2684-5ddf-5ab8-899b-a139d2958aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718823} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff357bcb-362e-56bd-a176-940829967a8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "91bf0e91-bd24-5db1-92d0-2b829d0800db" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=3 x + y - 2 z$, where $x=3 s^{2} + t$, $y=s^{2} + 4 t^{2}$, $z=- s + 2 t^{2}$. Calculate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}$ in terms of $s$ and $t$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/b5/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nHold $s$ fixed. Multiply along the three paths and add:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\cdot \\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\cdot \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\cdot \\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial t}\n$$\n\nFirst find the outer partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=3 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite these partials in terms of $s$ and $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=3 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each intermediate variable with respect to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}&=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}&=8 t \\\\ \\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial t}&=4 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the matching factors, then collect terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}&=\\left(3\\right)\\left(1\\right) \\\\ &{}+\\left(1\\right)\\left(8 t\\right) \\\\ &{}+\\left(-2\\right)\\left(4 t\\right) \\\\ &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718824 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1abc85d5-86f0-5217-9d6e-96c7860453fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\left(2 s - 1\\right) e^{- s^{2} + 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718807} {:answer/id #uuid "2eb224aa-3b89-52c3-8c2b-b1a75bfa5ae1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718809} {:answer/id #uuid "36ae4c4e-e185-56b1-b08a-0df06be0a631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\left(2 s + 1\\right) e^{- s^{2} + 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718810} {:answer/id #uuid "6713872d-a41b-558f-9f2b-b06748ac4ad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 s e^{- s^{2} + 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718814} {:answer/id #uuid "d715728e-d394-5cbf-bf32-d7fc5a439d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 s e^{- s^{2} + 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6713872d-a41b-558f-9f2b-b06748ac4ad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 s e^{- s^{2} + 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718814} :answer-field/id #uuid "13976d8d-4649-543f-9765-502e692bc36f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9b5dbbf3-66dc-59cb-b778-3d943b817542" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=e^{x + y + z}$, where $x=s + 2 t$, $y=- s + t$, $z=- s^{2}$. Calculate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}$ in terms of $s$ and $t$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nHold $t$ fixed. Multiply along the three paths and add:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\cdot \\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial s}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\cdot \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial s}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\cdot \\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial s}\n$$\n\nFirst find the outer partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=e^{x + y + z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=e^{x + y + z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=e^{x + y + z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite these partials in terms of $s$ and $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=e^{- s^{2} + 3 t} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=e^{- s^{2} + 3 t} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=e^{- s^{2} + 3 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each intermediate variable with respect to $s$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial s}&=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial s}&=-1 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial s}&=- 2 s\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the matching factors, then collect terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}&=\\left(e^{- s^{2} + 3 t}\\right)\\left(1\\right) \\\\ &{}+\\left(e^{- s^{2} + 3 t}\\right)\\left(-1\\right) \\\\ &{}+\\left(e^{- s^{2} + 3 t}\\right)\\left(- 2 s\\right) \\\\ &=- 2 s e^{- s^{2} + 3 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718830 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d50dfc2-fa3f-5be7-9e27-8d8990520eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\left(2 t - 1\\right) e^{- s - 2 t^{2} + t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718808} {:answer/id #uuid "580dbff9-7b4d-59da-aa98-5062a91765ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\left(4 t + 1\\right) e^{- s - 2 t^{2} + t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718813} {:answer/id #uuid "767a636e-39e7-58b8-bac9-5a34151697fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 t e^{- s - 2 t^{2} + t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718819} {:answer/id #uuid "b416643b-8776-5f4e-bad2-bf3390ccc619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\left(4 t - 3\\right) e^{- s - 2 t^{2} + t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718827} {:answer/id #uuid "e161dce9-70e7-5dd8-99e1-b8ebd87233a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\left(4 t - 1\\right) e^{- s - 2 t^{2} + t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e161dce9-70e7-5dd8-99e1-b8ebd87233a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\left(4 t - 1\\right) e^{- s - 2 t^{2} + t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718834} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c27478b-ebfb-54a8-aea6-2537c3942f8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718805}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d3b56182-44f1-555e-94cf-1b92945aa054" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=e^{x + y + z}$, where $x=- 2 s + 2 t$, $y=- 2 t^{2}$, $z=s - t$. Calculate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}$ in terms of $s$ and $t$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/b5/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nHold $s$ fixed. Multiply along the three paths and add:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\cdot \\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\cdot \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\cdot \\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial t}\n$$\n\nFirst find the outer partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=e^{x + y + z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=e^{x + y + z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=e^{x + y + z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite these partials in terms of $s$ and $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=e^{- s - 2 t^{2} + t} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=e^{- s - 2 t^{2} + t} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=e^{- s - 2 t^{2} + t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each intermediate variable with respect to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}&=2 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}&=- 4 t \\\\ \\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial t}&=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the matching factors, then collect terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}&=\\left(e^{- s - 2 t^{2} + t}\\right)\\left(2\\right) \\\\ &{}+\\left(e^{- s - 2 t^{2} + t}\\right)\\left(- 4 t\\right) \\\\ &{}+\\left(e^{- s - 2 t^{2} + t}\\right)\\left(-1\\right) \\\\ &=- \\left(4 t - 1\\right) e^{- s - 2 t^{2} + t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718833 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38e6133e-f2e8-585c-a138-5a92aeb192ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 t \\left(2 s + 1\\right) e^{- 2 s - 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718811} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce4f859-8687-578a-9fa9-b9413a1d2887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 t \\left(2 s + 1\\right) e^{- 2 s - 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718816} {:answer/id #uuid "af77cf1b-ce50-5b28-87d1-107f7e5f9887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 t \\left(s - 1\\right) e^{- 2 s - 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718825} {:answer/id #uuid "b0d6fae5-9a49-5bd1-8082-bc706e559970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 t \\left(2 s - 1\\right) e^{- 2 s - 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718826} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c7a3d7-cb8c-5ee0-918f-ca0887b37cba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 t \\left(2 s - 1\\right) e^{- 2 s - 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1c7a3d7-cb8c-5ee0-918f-ca0887b37cba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 t \\left(2 s - 1\\right) e^{- 2 s - 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718828} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6d4a5fe-06ae-5607-8a8c-1c16b37de381" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df6cbfbb-0ea4-51de-95d9-44441bbed429" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=x y z$, where $x=s e^{- 3 t}$, $y=-2$, $z=t e^{- 2 s}$. Calculate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}$ in terms of $s$ and $t$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nHold $t$ fixed. Multiply along the three paths and add:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\cdot \\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial s}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\cdot \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial s}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\cdot \\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial s}\n$$\n\nFirst find the outer partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=y z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=x z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=x y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite these partials in terms of $s$ and $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=- 2 t e^{- 2 s} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=s t e^{- 2 s - 3 t} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=- 2 s e^{- 3 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each intermediate variable with respect to $s$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial s}&=e^{- 3 t} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial s}&=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial s}&=- 2 t e^{- 2 s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine exponential factors using $e^A e^B=e^{A+B}$ when collecting the path products. Substitute the matching factors, then collect terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}&=\\left(- 2 t e^{- 2 s}\\right)\\left(e^{- 3 t}\\right) \\\\ &{}+\\left(s t e^{- 2 s - 3 t}\\right)\\left(0\\right) \\\\ &{}+\\left(- 2 s e^{- 3 t}\\right)\\left(- 2 t e^{- 2 s}\\right) \\\\ &=2 t \\left(2 s - 1\\right) e^{- 2 s - 3 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10c65f13-b75b-5193-8a68-e2ce29b230c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t \\cos{(t )} \\cos{(t^{2} )}\\\\&{}+(2 \\sin{(t )} \\sin{(t^{2} )})\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718846} {:answer/id #uuid "bd1d25cd-5d36-56b7-9821-8e26c3674720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&2 t \\sin{(t^{2} )} \\cos{(t )}\\\\&{}+(- t \\sin{(t )} \\sin{(t^{2} )})\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718864} {:answer/id #uuid "dba31d72-06b4-5740-8460-4fcc7fca4547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t \\cos{(t )} \\cos{(t^{2} )}\\\\&{}+(\\sin{(t )} \\sin{(t^{2} )})\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718867} {:answer/id #uuid "e418177a-caad-52e4-abbd-63e702bb56e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&2 t^{3} \\cos{(t )} \\cos{(t^{2} )}\\\\&{}+(\\sin{(t )} \\sin{(t^{2} )})\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718870} {:answer/id #uuid "f1ddb08f-7cf5-598f-8898-4ed59d16ee52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&2 t \\sin{(t^{2} )} \\cos{(t )}\\\\&{}+(2 \\sin{(t )} \\sin{(t^{2} )})\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dba31d72-06b4-5740-8460-4fcc7fca4547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t \\cos{(t )} \\cos{(t^{2} )}\\\\&{}+(\\sin{(t )} \\sin{(t^{2} )})\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718867} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d562e10-04c8-5632-bc12-c726527499a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718858}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0796b1a1-4393-544a-a2b5-bfeee4795248" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\sin{(x )} \\cos{(y )}$, $x=- t^{2}$ and $y=- t$, compute $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}t}$ in terms of $t$." :question/worked-solution "![Two chain-rule paths through x and y to t](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nMultiply along each path and add the contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the partial derivatives, holding the other intermediate variable constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\cos{(x )} \\cos{(y )} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- \\sin{(x )} \\sin{(y )}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the negative arguments, use $\\sin(-u)=-\\sin(u)$ and $\\cos(-u)=\\cos(u)$.\n\nSubstitute both coordinate functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\cos{((- t^{2}) )} \\cos{((- t) )} \\\\ &=\\cos{(t )} \\cos{(t^{2} )} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- \\sin{((- t^{2}) )} \\sin{((- t) )} \\\\ &=- \\sin{(t )} \\sin{(t^{2} )}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the coordinate functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=- 2 t \\\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCompute each path product, then add.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=(\\cos{(t )} \\cos{(t^{2} )})(- 2 t) \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=(- \\sin{(t )} \\sin{(t^{2} )})(-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}t}&=\\begin{aligned}&- 2 t \\cos{(t )} \\cos{(t^{2} )}\\\\&{}+(\\sin{(t )} \\sin{(t^{2} )})\\end{aligned}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718851 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04fc750b-f538-5d8b-ba73-1889ffdfefea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{2 s}{s + 1}\\\\&{}+\\left(- \\frac{s^{2}}{(s + 1)^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718843} {:answer/id #uuid "06929198-1d03-5b56-8e72-715c19715f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&- \\frac{2 s}{s + 1}\\\\&{}+\\left(- \\frac{s^{3}}{(s + 1)^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718844} {:answer/id #uuid "1c40840d-3863-5d18-b4f6-52b277cb3caa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&- \\frac{2 s}{s + 1}\\\\&{}+\\left(\\frac{1}{s + 1}\\right)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718847} {:answer/id #uuid "3ec93699-2355-5427-86f8-c67feb675d3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{2 s}{s + 1}\\\\&{}+\\left(- \\frac{s^{3}}{(s + 1)^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718853} {:answer/id #uuid "8bb51e85-0a3a-527d-8f20-f665ef4b12f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{1}{s + 1}\\\\&{}+\\left(\\frac{1}{s + 1}\\right)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04fc750b-f538-5d8b-ba73-1889ffdfefea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{2 s}{s + 1}\\\\&{}+\\left(- \\frac{s^{2}}{(s + 1)^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718843} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7c6876a-bee9-5b18-98f9-c1ce6f9c29a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2dca0f14-3fe0-5a5a-b8ba-6e56fd4b4fe3" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y + 1}$, $x=s^{2}$ and $y=s$, compute $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}s}$ in terms of $s$. Assume $s + 1\\ne0$." :question/worked-solution "![Two chain-rule paths through x and y to s](images/7e/7e5b5001794ecdf2c9b9e9102f334a63d2c59bc6f7511c2eb7fa358fc94cb0c5.png)\n\nMultiply along each path and add the contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}s}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}s}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the partial derivatives, holding the other intermediate variable constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{1}{y + 1} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- \\frac{x}{(y + 1)^{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinate functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{1}{s + 1} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- \\frac{s^{2}}{(s + 1)^{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the coordinate functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=2 s \\\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCompute each path product, then add.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=\\left(\\frac{1}{s + 1}\\right)(2 s) \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=\\left(- \\frac{s^{2}}{(s + 1)^{2}}\\right)(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{2 s}{s + 1}\\\\&{}+\\left(- \\frac{s^{2}}{(s + 1)^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718854 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0261bed0-2e20-5107-80ad-900bbfbda7c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&- \\cos{(s )}\\\\&{}+(- 3 \\cos{(s )})\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718841} {:answer/id #uuid "298ef34e-0394-5b27-aee4-f388020a0397" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&- \\cos{(s )}\\\\&{}+(9 s \\sin{(s )})\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718850} {:answer/id #uuid "5a4e7840-668f-58f3-a219-5fa96157e165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&3 \\cos{(s )}\\\\&{}+(3 s \\sin{(s )})\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718855} {:answer/id #uuid "ae70a6bd-e054-5e7b-99bb-2cde5a396863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&- 3 \\cos{(s )}\\\\&{}+(- 3 \\cos{(s )})\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718862} {:answer/id #uuid "e0052cd7-1693-51ef-be53-e68083c5c3c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&- 3 \\cos{(s )}\\\\&{}+(3 s \\sin{(s )})\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0052cd7-1693-51ef-be53-e68083c5c3c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&- 3 \\cos{(s )}\\\\&{}+(3 s \\sin{(s )})\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718869} :answer-field/id #uuid "75ac6cfc-e243-54f5-9758-75052fcbd301" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718856}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4d4c35df-57cc-5aa2-a8ac-fee89410bca1" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x \\cos{(y )}$, $x=- 3 s$ and $y=- s$, compute $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}s}$ in terms of $s$." :question/worked-solution "![Two chain-rule paths through x and y to s](images/7e/7e5b5001794ecdf2c9b9e9102f334a63d2c59bc6f7511c2eb7fa358fc94cb0c5.png)\n\nMultiply along each path and add the contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}s}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}s}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the partial derivatives, holding the other intermediate variable constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\cos{(y )} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- x \\sin{(y )}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the negative arguments, use $\\sin(-u)=-\\sin(u)$ and $\\cos(-u)=\\cos(u)$.\n\nSubstitute both coordinate functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\cos{((- s) )} \\\\ &=\\cos{(s )} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- (- 3 s) \\sin{((- s) )} \\\\ &=- 3 s \\sin{(s )}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the coordinate functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=-3 \\\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCompute each path product, then add.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=(\\cos{(s )})(-3) \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=(- 3 s \\sin{(s )})(-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=\\begin{aligned}&- 3 \\cos{(s )}\\\\&{}+(3 s \\sin{(s )})\\end{aligned}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718865 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20631966-cb9f-58e4-acf0-6868c0fe99b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&2 \\ln{(2 s )}\\\\&{}+(0)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718848} {:answer/id #uuid "3c1a1be3-ad0d-5c6a-90f1-95b5986f22c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&4\\\\&{}+(4)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718852} {:answer/id #uuid "a5edb743-2921-58a1-a57d-3147999e5b93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&2 \\ln{(2 s )}\\\\&{}+(4)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718861} {:answer/id #uuid "b6650493-14b7-5418-bc8b-f69e915c77f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&4\\\\&{}+\\left(\\frac{2 s \\ln{(2 s )} + 2 s}{s}\\right)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718863} {:answer/id #uuid "e9c15ffe-7dcb-5904-96b0-95a35b46d20d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{2 s \\ln{(2 s )} + 2 s}{s}\\\\&{}+(0)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5edb743-2921-58a1-a57d-3147999e5b93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&2 \\ln{(2 s )}\\\\&{}+(4)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718861} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd3f3baa-7255-5131-beeb-1193786d7e87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718868}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4d27b94-58f2-53bd-bc90-c4c9864cb49e" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x \\ln{(y )} + y$, $x=2 s$ and $y=2 s$, compute $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}s}$ in terms of $s$. Assume $s>0$." :question/worked-solution "![Two chain-rule paths through x and y to s](images/7e/7e5b5001794ecdf2c9b9e9102f334a63d2c59bc6f7511c2eb7fa358fc94cb0c5.png)\n\nMultiply along each path and add the contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}s}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}s}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the partial derivatives, holding the other intermediate variable constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\ln{(y )} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{x}{y} + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinate functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\ln{(2 s )} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the coordinate functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=2 \\\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCompute each path product, then add.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=(\\ln{(2 s )})(2) \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=(2)(2) \\\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=\\begin{aligned}&2 \\ln{(2 s )}\\\\&{}+(4)\\end{aligned}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718875 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04498d38-9fab-5be4-8280-b4b2f8860e4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 2 \\ln{(2 s )} + (2)}{\\sqrt{2(2 s)(\\ln{(2 s )})}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718842} {:answer/id #uuid "220bfd4e-05f4-5361-bb84-86efc5a12134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\ln{(2 s )} + (2)}{\\sqrt{2(2 s)(\\ln{(2 s )})}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718849} {:answer/id #uuid "964e3e20-0cbc-568b-a76e-de6925b12777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\ln{(2 s )} + (-2)}{\\sqrt{2(2 s)(\\ln{(2 s )})}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718859} {:answer/id #uuid "a11d0ed2-a366-5376-926f-c2325bb36219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 2 \\ln{(2 s )} + \\left(\\frac{4 s \\ln{(2 s )}}{s \\ln{(2 s )}}\\right)}{\\sqrt{2(2 s)(\\ln{(2 s )})}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718860} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b00de5-dc90-575c-bd48-1a92653f9a0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\ln{(2 s )} + (-2)}{\\sqrt{2(2 s)(\\ln{(2 s )})}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "220bfd4e-05f4-5361-bb84-86efc5a12134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\ln{(2 s )} + (2)}{\\sqrt{2(2 s)(\\ln{(2 s )})}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718849} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4fa83e4-45a7-5708-8c27-bbb82e71ce4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd0c4e9f-278d-5069-a7ca-5f29b3963717" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{2xy}$, $x=2 s$ and $y=\\ln{(2 s )}$, compute $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}s}$ in terms of $s$. Assume $s>0$ and $2 s>1$." :question/worked-solution "![Two chain-rule paths through x and y to s](images/7e/7e5b5001794ecdf2c9b9e9102f334a63d2c59bc6f7511c2eb7fa358fc94cb0c5.png)\n\nMultiply along each path and add the contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}s}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}s}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the partial derivatives, holding the other intermediate variable constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{2xy}} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2xy}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinate functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{\\ln{(2 s )}}{\\sqrt{2(2 s)(\\ln{(2 s )})}} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{2 s}{\\sqrt{2(2 s)(\\ln{(2 s )})}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the coordinate functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=2 \\\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=\\frac{1}{s}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCompute each path product, then add.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=\\left(\\frac{\\ln{(2 s )}}{\\sqrt{2(2 s)(\\ln{(2 s )})}}\\right)(2) \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=\\left(\\frac{2 s}{\\sqrt{2(2 s)(\\ln{(2 s )})}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{s}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}s}&=\\frac{2 \\ln{(2 s )} + (2)}{\\sqrt{2(2 s)(\\ln{(2 s )})}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718902 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00b269ba-0e75-53ed-86f1-b6b96edcd763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718900} {:answer/id #uuid "2d74a82e-118b-5101-86d9-cd667ee806a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718904} {:answer/id #uuid "4d879fdf-1a05-5615-ab56-83dbf4db66e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718909} {:answer/id #uuid "a8073d16-58e9-5af9-ad61-2f25b6afb8fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718921} {:answer/id #uuid "e2ff96c6-167a-5b21-b9a4-b8986640c732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d74a82e-118b-5101-86d9-cd667ee806a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718904} :answer-field/id #uuid "7095d691-0405-5208-bc67-82eb7c51cc85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0cc27e81-41c2-5213-9930-95a58f087161" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F&=\\bigl(a x y^{2}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &{}+\\bigl(2 x^{2} y + 3\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j\\end{aligned}\n$$\non $\\mathbb R^2$, where $a$ is a constant. Given that $\\mathbf F$ is conservative, find $a$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$. Both components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. On this domain, the conservative-field test is $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nThe required partial derivatives are\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=2 a x y \\\\ Q_x&=4 x y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquality must hold for every point of the plane. Simplifying this identity gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a - 2&=0 \\\\ a&=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe matching terms cancel as identities. Any common factor that vanishes at some points is nonzero elsewhere; equality at those zeros alone would not determine the constant.\n\nAt $a=2$, the two displayed partial derivatives agree everywhere, so this value satisfies the conservative-field condition."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718908 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c0a2a57-5a16-531c-b2c7-67e3bfd7ce87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718901} {:answer/id #uuid "7fe449ba-6b95-5065-b238-4f2752d19895" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718916} {:answer/id #uuid "eb5d0a86-6352-5fc2-b205-cb616f22804a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718931} {:answer/id #uuid "eb6d9a98-7bdd-5301-b111-b78ed023ed4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718932} {:answer/id #uuid "fd80168c-a9c8-5879-adcb-3673ff554b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fe449ba-6b95-5065-b238-4f2752d19895" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718916} :answer-field/id #uuid "9282840c-6722-5980-884a-868ab068a023" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718920}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "48620377-1760-55a7-bd75-578121d62441" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F&=\\bigl(y e^{y + x} - 2 x^{2}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &{}+\\bigl(- 2 y^{2} + \\left(- 2 a + y\\right) e^{y + x}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j\\end{aligned}\n$$\non $\\mathbb R^2$, where $a$ is a constant. Given that $\\mathbf F$ is conservative, find $a$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$. Both components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. On this domain, the conservative-field test is $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nThe required partial derivatives are\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=y e^{y + x} + e^{y + x} \\\\ Q_x&=\\left(- 2 a + y\\right) e^{y + x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquality must hold for every point of the plane. Simplifying this identity gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 a + 1&=0 \\\\ a&=- \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe matching terms cancel as identities. Any common factor that vanishes at some points is nonzero elsewhere; equality at those zeros alone would not determine the constant.\n\nAt $a=- \\frac{1}{2}$, the two displayed partial derivatives agree everywhere, so this value satisfies the conservative-field condition."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718919 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44c4b278-922f-5205-85c5-532feae4989f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718906} {:answer/id #uuid "81e26897-a317-5095-908d-79cdd7afc2db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718917} {:answer/id #uuid "cd736a52-58cd-5305-aac2-cb1ae32ee360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718926} {:answer/id #uuid "ce19a6ce-50f5-5939-be32-f87940ab8587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718927} {:answer/id #uuid "dc0e3fc3-9f07-59b2-b2c0-f4bcdfbe83b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd736a52-58cd-5305-aac2-cb1ae32ee360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718926} :answer-field/id #uuid "462ad542-e51e-52d2-8f5d-880d942561f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f018618-7caf-55fe-9857-b8adeee91f92" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F&=\\bigl(- 6 y^{2} x^{2}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &{}+\\bigl(a x - 4 y x^{3}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j\\end{aligned}\n$$\non $\\mathbb R^2$, where $a$ is a constant. Given that $\\mathbf F$ is conservative, find $a$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$. Both components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. On this domain, the conservative-field test is $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nThe required partial derivatives are\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=- 12 y x^{2} \\\\ Q_x&=a - 12 y x^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquality must hold for every point of the plane. Simplifying this identity gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a&=0 \\\\ a&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe matching terms cancel as identities. Any common factor that vanishes at some points is nonzero elsewhere; equality at those zeros alone would not determine the constant.\n\nAt $a=0$, the two displayed partial derivatives agree everywhere, so this value satisfies the conservative-field condition."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718924 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "606cb868-8f00-54c9-8ef4-f0f79bce87a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 \\pi - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718913} {:answer/id #uuid "7673240e-e466-5a1a-9760-91589db368f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 \\pi - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718915} {:answer/id #uuid "bc0d480e-e3b5-5c91-bdfd-b3d708132986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718922} {:answer/id #uuid "e89bd4f3-d778-556f-ba89-04bd29db8639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718930} {:answer/id #uuid "f74c7d33-be14-5db9-9578-f32384e1bd21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e89bd4f3-d778-556f-ba89-04bd29db8639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718930} :answer-field/id #uuid "50b8fde8-e28c-5cea-bafe-3b8494bbc6f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c44ba436-9f71-5ce1-a80e-aa7b0b05c518" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F&=\\bigl(6 x^{2} + \\cos{\\left(4 \\pi y \\right)}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &{}+\\bigl(a x - 4 \\pi x \\sin{\\left(4 \\pi y \\right)} + 3 x + 3 y^{2}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j\\end{aligned}\n$$\non $\\mathbb R^2$, where $a$ is a constant. Given that $\\mathbf F$ is conservative, find $a$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$. Both components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. On this domain, the conservative-field test is $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nThe required partial derivatives are\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=- 4 \\pi \\sin{\\left(4 \\pi y \\right)} \\\\ Q_x&=a - 4 \\pi \\sin{\\left(4 \\pi y \\right)} + 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquality must hold for every point of the plane. Simplifying this identity gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a + 3&=0 \\\\ a&=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe matching terms cancel as identities. Any common factor that vanishes at some points is nonzero elsewhere; equality at those zeros alone would not determine the constant.\n\nAt $a=-3$, the two displayed partial derivatives agree everywhere, so this value satisfies the conservative-field condition."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718925 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dbb5d18-641e-5005-8531-a440cc751eef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718905} {:answer/id #uuid "4f7df823-bbad-5884-9e63-750b88c55d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718910} {:answer/id #uuid "5db1aab4-25c3-5fa3-bcec-5ccf45c66712" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718912} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf019b4-f77a-5a84-84bb-66e81a6b5379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718918} {:answer/id #uuid "c3d197a8-0ff1-549b-9b94-9f5d4f698c5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dbb5d18-641e-5005-8531-a440cc751eef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718905} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dbac4d7-ce42-53c7-8362-5905185dc016" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c9919d05-47f4-5402-9a3a-405fe8189a25" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F&=\\bigl(9 y x^{2} + 2 y + 3 x^{2}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &{}+\\bigl(- a x + 3 y^{2} + 3 x^{3}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j\\end{aligned}\n$$\non $\\mathbb R^2$, where $a$ is a constant. Given that $\\mathbf F$ is conservative, find $a$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$. Both components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. On this domain, the conservative-field test is $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nThe required partial derivatives are\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=9 x^{2} + 2 \\\\ Q_x&=- a + 9 x^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquality must hold for every point of the plane. Simplifying this identity gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- a - 2&=0 \\\\ a&=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe matching terms cancel as identities. Any common factor that vanishes at some points is nonzero elsewhere; equality at those zeros alone would not determine the constant.\n\nAt $a=-2$, the two displayed partial derivatives agree everywhere, so this value satisfies the conservative-field condition."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98e1acb1-b174-5b5a-94b1-d5ef18fe3bde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719001} {:answer/id #uuid "abfdf992-03e3-5674-abe6-2d29df93bae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719006} {:answer/id #uuid "b7a9bc3d-6dcc-5825-8c03-fe5263506031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719007} {:answer/id #uuid "dd86f88b-c3d8-5326-b335-178a40df994f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719013} {:answer/id #uuid "e3eea4bf-9762-52f5-97d9-f7098f735d8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abfdf992-03e3-5674-abe6-2d29df93bae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719006} :answer-field/id #uuid "7865fdde-66dd-5fb7-bf92-6ab1b86a054e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "230efcd0-4973-5343-be47-ee6f3cc55114" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F&=\\bigl(9 y^{2} x + 25 y + x^{2}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &{}+\\bigl(a^{2} y x^{2} + y^{2} + x \\left(a + 2\\right)^{2}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j\\end{aligned}\n$$\non $\\mathbb R^2$, where $a$ is a constant. Given that $\\mathbf F$ is conservative, find $a$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$. Both components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. On this domain, the conservative-field test is $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nThe required partial derivatives are\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=18 y x + 25 \\\\ Q_x&=2 a^{2} y x + \\left(a + 2\\right)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquality is an identity in $x$ and $y$, so the coefficient of $xy$ and the constant term must both agree:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a^2&=9 \\\\ \\left(a + 2\\right)^{2}&=25\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe first condition gives $a=-3$ or $a=3$. The second gives $a=3$ or $a=-7$. Their only common value is $a=3$. The opposite root of the first condition fails the constant-term condition; the other root of the second fails the coefficient condition.\n\nAt $a=3$, the two displayed partial derivatives agree everywhere, so this value satisfies the conservative-field condition."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719002 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29d32fff-3c5e-570b-97f3-634b505b447d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718993} {:answer/id #uuid "54454d2c-e398-50bd-b2ff-56c0af33930e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718995} {:answer/id #uuid "943b683f-d77b-561f-9167-1055187fcb3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719000} {:answer/id #uuid "dc7a223f-bcef-57f9-bfa7-17affde216df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719012} {:answer/id #uuid "ff899a17-1214-5009-affe-6ede9d7867bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "943b683f-d77b-561f-9167-1055187fcb3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719000} :answer-field/id #uuid "10211473-7b30-58cd-a3c9-1635cb3a6713" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "992672ac-7d59-5d8c-8560-a621042fe3b0" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F&=\\bigl(a^{2} x y^{2} - x^{2} + y \\left(a + 2\\right)^{2}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &{}+\\bigl(16 x^{2} y + 4 x - y^{2}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j\\end{aligned}\n$$\non $\\mathbb R^2$, where $a$ is a constant. Given that $\\mathbf F$ is conservative, find $a$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$. Both components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. On this domain, the conservative-field test is $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nThe required partial derivatives are\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=2 a^{2} x y + \\left(a + 2\\right)^{2} \\\\ Q_x&=32 x y + 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquality is an identity in $x$ and $y$, so the coefficient of $xy$ and the constant term must both agree:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a^2&=16 \\\\ \\left(a + 2\\right)^{2}&=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe first condition gives $a=-4$ or $a=4$. The second gives $a=-4$ or $a=0$. Their only common value is $a=-4$. The opposite root of the first condition fails the constant-term condition; the other root of the second fails the coefficient condition.\n\nAt $a=-4$, the two displayed partial derivatives agree everywhere, so this value satisfies the conservative-field condition."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14745cee-4a6c-5e5e-a976-c50b87d43070" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718991} {:answer/id #uuid "72fb06e2-ef18-5f44-a90f-55a589628fb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718996} {:answer/id #uuid "915d6282-0015-545c-9065-ca3ae54aaa79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718998} {:answer/id #uuid "c8757d0f-2b00-54a2-9f3a-bf492264c3bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719009} {:answer/id #uuid "d8316569-f0e0-5678